{"parentUuid":"14ccd525-79ab-4c63-8710-df1325b884d1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"adab621f-8365-4b99-847d-20d9fa3c297c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"can you take a look at this review for the current branch: \n\n# Review 01\n\n> Status: pending-dev\n> Date: 2026-04-22\n> Reviewer: Code Review Agent\n> Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES\n\n## Scope\n\nReviewed branch `feat/entire-review` against `main`. The feature introduces a new\n`entire review` command that runs configured review skills inside a single\nagent session, with the session/checkpoint metadata recording that a review\noccurred.\n\n- 17 commits, ~1,750 lines across 30 files (code + tests + CLAUDE.md).\n- Key files: `cmd/entire/cli/review.go` (+685), `cmd/entire/cli/review_test.go`\n  (+395), `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go` + test (+186), plus additions to\n  `session.State`, `settings.EntireSettings.Review`, `checkpoint` types (`Kind`,\n  `ReviewSkills`, `HasReview`), `trailers`, and three agent `Launcher` impls.\n- `mise run test` — all packages pass.\n- `mise run lint` — 0 issues.\n\nPrevious PR-level reviewer feedback (commit `47eb589` \"Address PR review\nfeedback\") has been addressed. No prior `review-NN.md` files exist in this\nrepo; this is the first file-based review.\n\n## High (Must Fix)\n\n1. **High: the unsupported-launcher fallback clears the pending marker it\n   just told the user to rely on.** In\n   [review.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_worktree1/cmd/entire/cli/review.go:414),\n   the cleanup `defer` is installed before the `LauncherFor` check, and the\n   fallback path at\n   [review.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_worktree1/cmd/entire/cli/review.go:425)\n   returns `nil`. That means configs for non-launchable agents print\n   \"falling back to --track-only\", but the marker is removed on return, so\n   the manually started review session will not be tagged or condensed as a\n   review.\n\n   Fix: either skip the defer-driven cleanup on this branch (e.g. move the\n   \"fallback to track-only\" return *above* the defer, analogous to how the\n   `trackOnly` branch at line 400-406 already does), or short-circuit the\n   cleanup with a local flag (`markerHandedOff := false; defer ... if !markerHandedOff ...`).\n   Add a test that registers a non-Launcher agent and asserts the marker\n   survives when `LauncherFor` returns `ok=false`.\n\n## Important (Should Fix)\n\n2. **Medium: `entire review` never verifies that hooks are installed for\n   the configured agent before launching it.** The command selects an\n   agent from settings in\n   [review.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_worktree1/cmd/entire/cli/review.go:353)\n   and immediately writes the marker / launches, but there is no\n   `AreHooksInstalled` gate even though the feature depends on\n   `UserPromptSubmit` adoption and the repo already has\n   [GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_worktree1/cmd/entire/cli/config.go:85).\n   A manually edited config such as `\"claude-code\": [...]` in a repo\n   without `entire enable` will appear to run successfully, but no review\n   metadata will ever be recorded because no hook fires.\n\n   Focused tests passed: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/... -run 'Review|AdoptPendingReviewMarker|DetectBaseBranch|DetectReviewScope'`\n   and `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/... -run 'LaunchCmd|LauncherFor'`.\n   Those scenarios are not currently covered by tests.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/review.go:451-468] Multi-agent review config silently\n  prefers the alphabetically-first agent, with no override.**\n  `selectReviewAgent` picks `sort.Strings(names)[0]`, so a user with\n  `{\"claude-code\": [...], \"codex\": [...]}` configured can never reach the\n  codex agent without removing `claude-code` from settings. The doc comment\n  admits \"v1: single agent\" but there's no flag to select an agent, and the\n  first-run picker happily writes multiple entries. Either (a) gate the\n  picker to one agent at a time, (b) add `--agent <name>`, or (c) prompt\n  the user when the map has multiple keys. Today the UX is \"I configured\n  codex and nothing happens,\" which will produce confused bug reports.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/review.go:425 → .github/hooks, etc.] Stale config can\n  point to an uninstalled agent.**\n  `runReviewConfigPicker` correctly gates to `GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled`,\n  but once saved, `runReview` reads `s.Review` directly with no re-check.\n  If the user later runs `entire disable` for an agent, its entry stays in\n  the settings map, `selectReviewAgent` will pick it, and the marker will be\n  written for an agent whose hook will never adopt it — same silent failure\n  as the Critical above. Suggest intersecting `s.Review` keys with\n  `GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled(ctx)` inside `runReview` and skipping/warning\n  on missing entries.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/review.go:196-201] Empty-installed-agents error message\n  assumes the fix is `entire enable`.**\n  The error says: `\"no agents installed; run 'entire enable' first\"`. In\n  practice a user who disabled a specific agent via `entire configure\n  --remove` may already have `entire enable`d the repo — they just don't\n  have hooks for any agent. Consider `\"no agents with hooks installed; run\n  'entire configure --agent <name>' to install hooks.\"`.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go:440-449] `HasReview` is not\n  derived from session metadata — stale summaries can never lose it, but\n  also never gain it on rewrite.**\n  `writeCheckpointSummary` carries `HasReview` forward from the existing\n  summary OR sets it from `opts.HasReview`. `reaggregateFromEntries`\n  recomputes `CheckpointsCount`/`FilesTouched`/`TokenUsage` by reading each\n  session's `CommittedMetadata` from the tree, but **does not** look at the\n  per-session `Kind` field. That means:\n  1. If the summary is ever rebuilt without `opts.HasReview=true` (e.g.\n     someone re-runs `CondenseSession` for a non-review session after a\n     review session was previously condensed), the flag *is* preserved via\n     the \"existing summary\" read — good.\n  2. But if the root `metadata.json` blob is missing or unreadable while\n     the session subfolder with `Kind=agent_review` survives, `HasReview`\n     silently resets to false.\n  This is unlikely in practice (the summary and session are written in the\n  same commit), but the truth-of-record should be the per-session\n  `CommittedMetadata.Kind`. Consider making `reaggregateFromEntries`\n  OR `writeCheckpointSummary` iterate the per-session metadata and\n  OR-in `Kind.IsReview()` equivalent. (Since `checkpoint` can't import\n  `session`, this would mean either hardcoding `\"agent_review\"` in the\n  checkpoint package or adding a small `IsReviewKind(string) bool` helper\n  exported from `session` that's safe for `checkpoint` to consume.)\n\n- **README.md + CHANGELOG.md — feature is undocumented for end users.**\n  CLAUDE.md has extensive documentation, but `README.md` lists every other\n  `entire` command in the Commands Reference table and doesn't mention\n  `entire review`. `CHANGELOG.md` has no entry for this feature. If the\n  command is intentionally preview/hidden, mark the cobra command\n  `Hidden: true` and add a changelog \"preview\" note. Otherwise, add a\n  README section and a CHANGELOG entry before release.\n\n## Suggestions (Consider)\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/review.go:54-60] `pendingMarkerPath` discards\n  `session.SessionStateDirName` collision risk.**\n  The marker lives next to per-session `<session-id>.json` files under\n  `.git/entire-sessions/`. The filename is a constant (`review-pending.json`)\n  that could collide with a real session ID. Validation prevents\n  path-traversal, but defense-in-depth: pick a reserved prefix (e.g.\n  `.review-pending.json`) that session-ID validation would reject anyway.\n  Very low risk — session IDs are `YYYY-MM-DD-<UUID>` — but a future refactor\n  that loosens validation could expose this.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/review.go:126-139] `curatedReviewSkills` is a hardcoded\n  map with no update path.**\n  Only `claude-code` and `codex` have curated skills. New agents (or new\n  skills for existing ones) require a code change. Consider loading from an\n  embed-ed JSON or from agent-specific files so community skills can ship\n  without a CLI release.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/review.go:481-491] `currentHeadSHA` duplicates git logic\n  already available via `go-git`.**\n  The rest of the codebase uses `git.PlainOpen(...).Head()`. Shelling out\n  is not wrong here (consistency with `detectReviewScope`), but the helper\n  could be a one-liner `repo.Head().Hash().String()` without spawning a\n  subprocess. Minor.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/review.go:195-292] `runReviewConfigPicker` does not test\n  coverage for accessible mode.**\n  `NewAccessibleForm` is used, but no test exercises the `ACCESSIBLE=1`\n  path, so regressions in accessible rendering would slip through. A\n  lightweight test that sets `ACCESSIBLE=1` and verifies the form doesn't\n  panic would be worth adding.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go:271-289] Non-atomic read-modify-write on\n  session state during marker adoption.**\n  Load → mutate → Save with no lock around the file. If two concurrent\n  `UserPromptSubmit` hooks adopt simultaneously, both could win because the\n  first save is clobbered by the second. Concurrent hooks for the same\n  session ID are unlikely in practice (agents serialize hooks per turn),\n  but adding a quick `fcntl`-style advisory lock would be cheap insurance.\n  Same shape of issue exists elsewhere in the codebase, so not a blocker.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/review.go:451-468] `selectReviewAgent` returns\n  `([]string(nil), errors.New(\"...\"))` twice with the same error text.**\n  Collapse the two branches into a single \"filter to valid entries, then\n  sort\" step to avoid the duplicated error string.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/review.go:302-318] Flag documentation drift risk.**\n  The command `Long` text mentions `--edit` but not `--track-only`. Easy\n  fix: mention `--track-only` in the long description, or trust the flag\n  registration to speak for itself.\n\n## Praise\n\n- **Excellent defensive commentary throughout `review.go`.** Almost every\n  non-trivial decision is justified in a comment — the worktree-scoped\n  marker rationale (lines 141-147, 173-179), the settings-wipe data-loss\n  guard (lines 330-341, 667-684), the defer-cleanup lifecycle (lines\n  408-422). This raises the bar for future maintainers. Exactly the \"teach\n  via code\" pattern the reviewer guide asks for.\n\n- **Worktree-scoped marker is a real correctness win.**\n  `TestAdoptPendingReviewMarker_OtherWorktreeLeavesMarker` documents a race\n  that's hard to see until you hit it. The fix is minimal and the test\n  pins it — textbook.\n\n- **HasReview-via-Kind derivation.**\n  `session.Kind.IsReview()` + `opts.HasReview: state.Kind.IsReview()` is\n  the right seam. Pins the invariant that new review kinds won't need\n  three string-literal updates across packages. `TestKindIsReview` makes\n  it load-bearing.\n\n- **Settings-malformed → surface error instead of clobbering.**\n  `TestSaveReviewConfig_ReturnsErrorOnMalformedSettings` is exactly the\n  regression shape you want pinned: the test asserts the file is byte-for-\n  byte identical before and after a failed save. That's the difference\n  between a close call and a data-loss bug.\n\n- **`detectBaseBranch` fallback order matches its doc comment, and is\n  tested.** Two regression tests\n  (`TestDetectBaseBranch_UsesOriginMainWhenNoLocalMain`,\n  `TestDetectBaseBranch_PrefersAllRemotesOverLocals`) pin the order so a\n  future refactor can't quietly flip it. The\n  `masterBaseBranch`/`defaultBaseBranch` constants are used consistently\n  across `git_operations.go`, `resume.go`, `review.go`.\n\n- **`Launcher` abstraction is cleanly scoped.** Three agent impls; a\n  single-line Launcher interface; `LauncherFor` is the exact ergonomic\n  helper callers need; `TestLauncher_AtLeastOneImplementor` ensures the\n  build can't regress into a state where no agent can be spawned.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe feature is well-engineered, thoroughly tested (394 lines of tests for\nthe review package alone, plus integration via `TestAdoptPendingReviewMarker*`\nin `lifecycle_test.go`), and the design choices (pending-marker + hook\nadoption, worktree scoping, HasReview umbrella flag, settings-malformed\nguard) reflect careful thinking. CLAUDE.md is updated correctly; lint +\nunit tests are green.\n\nThe High item — marker erasure on the `LauncherFor` `!ok` branch — is a\nreal bug that will silently break the fallback code path the commit\nmessages explicitly promise. It's a one-line fix plus a test. The Medium\nitem — no `AreHooksInstalled` gate — is the same silent-failure shape on\na different input path (manually edited config in a repo without\n`entire enable`).\n\nThe other \"Important\" items are quality-of-release issues (multi-agent\nselection UX, stale config, README/CHANGELOG). None block merge in the\nstrict sense, but the README/CHANGELOG gap will produce a version shipping\nan undocumented command.\n\nEstimated effort to address feedback: 2-3 hours (Critical fix + test + one\nImportant + docs).\n\n### Previous Review Status\n\nNo prior `review-NN.md` files. Upstream PR-review feedback (\"data-loss,\ncleanup, context, HasReview derivation,\" commit `47eb589`) appears fully\naddressed based on the current code and the dedicated regression tests:\n\n- [x] Settings-load errors no longer wipe user config (tested).\n- [x] Pending marker cleaned up on every spawn-path failure (via defer) —\n      *except* the `LauncherFor !ok` branch. See Critical above.\n- [x] `detectBaseBranch` prefers all remotes before any local (tested).\n- [x] `HasReview` derived from `session.Kind.IsReview()` (tested).\n- [x] Context threaded through marker I/O.\n- [x] `headHasReviewCheckpoint` logs at Debug on each failure step."},"uuid":"f339b4ab-e9e4-41da-9fc0-c73b5347d8d6","timestamp":"2026-04-22T08:14:21.006Z","permissionMode":"default","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
