{"parentUuid":"9dd0107c-00e0-46de-81da-48e2c257f194","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WELMjKNDkfuHhGkjBWERyN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## What `entire review` does\n\nIt runs a set of configured review skills inside a single agent session, and records — permanently, on the next `git commit` — that the code was reviewed and which skills were run. The review metadata rides along in the checkpoint alongside normal session metadata.\n\nIt does **not** track verdicts, status, or create empty commits. The session is just a fact, attached to whatever commit you make next.\n\n## The core idea: pending-marker + hook adoption\n\nThe command doesn't launch the agent and inject a special mode. Instead:\n\n1. `entire review` writes a small \"pending review\" marker file to `.git/entire-sessions/review-pending.json` — just the agent name, selected skills, starting SHA, worktree path, and a timestamp.\n2. It spawns (or tells you to manually start) the agent.\n3. When the agent fires its first `UserPromptSubmit` lifecycle hook, the hook handler calls `adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto`, which:\n   - Reads the marker.\n   - Checks the marker's `WorktreePath` matches the session's — so a marker written in worktree A isn't claimed by a session in worktree B (both share `.git/entire-sessions/`).\n   - Tags the session with `Kind = session.KindAgentReview` and stores the skills in `state.ReviewSkills`.\n   - Deletes the marker (so a later session doesn't inherit the tag).\n4. The agent runs the skills, the session ends naturally.\n5. On the next `git commit`, the PostCommit hook condenses the review session into the checkpoint on `entire/checkpoints/v1`. The per-session metadata carries `Kind: \"agent_review\"` and `ReviewSkills`; the root `CheckpointSummary` sets `HasReview: true` as the umbrella flag.\n\nThis means `entire review` has no new commit type, no new branch, no new condensation path — it piggybacks on the existing session → checkpoint → commit pipeline.\n\n## Flow inside `runReview`\n\n1. **Pre-flight** — must be in a git repo.\n2. **Load config** — reads `.entire/settings.json`. Malformed file surfaces an error instead of silently overwriting the user's other settings.\n3. **First-run picker** — if `review` config is missing, `runReviewConfigPicker` shows a `huh` multi-select per installed agent (only agents with curated skills in `curatedReviewSkills` are offered) and writes the selection back.\n4. **Agent selection** — `selectReviewAgent(review, --agent)`. With `--agent NAME`, picks that specific agent; otherwise alphabetically-first.\n5. **Hooks-installed gate** — aborts with a clear \"run `entire configure --agent <name>` first\" if the selected agent has no hooks installed (since nothing would ever adopt the marker).\n6. **Re-run guard** — reads HEAD's `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, resolves the checkpoint summary, checks `HasReview`. If the current HEAD is already reviewed, prompt \"Already reviewed… proceed anyway?\"\n7. **Resolve HEAD SHA + worktree root** and write the pending marker.\n8. **`--track-only` branch** — prints \"marker written; start the agent manually\" and returns. Marker persists.\n9. **Resolve `Launcher`** — if the selected agent has no `LaunchCmd` (cursor, opencode, copilot-cli, factoryai-droid), fall back to the same persist-marker behavior as `--track-only`. *Critically, this happens before the cleanup defer* so the marker survives for the user to adopt manually.\n10. **Cleanup defer** — on any error/exit past this point, if the marker is still there (the hook never adopted it — agent crashed, user `/quit`ed immediately), clear it so it doesn't mis-tag an unrelated future session.\n11. **Print scope** — a one-line `reviewScope` summary (branch vs base, ahead commits, files changed, uncommitted) via `git` shell-outs.\n12. **Compose prompt** (`\"Please run these review skills in order: 1. X 2. Y\"`) and launch the agent subprocess.\n\n## Flags\n\n- `--edit` — re-open the picker to modify the saved config.\n- `--track-only` — write the marker without spawning the agent (for when you want to start the agent yourself).\n- `--agent NAME` — pick a specific configured agent when you've configured more than one.\n\n## Where things live\n\n- Command: `cmd/entire/cli/review.go`\n- Marker adoption in the hook: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go:271-289`\n- `Launcher` interface: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` (implemented by `claudecode`, `codex`, `geminicli`)\n- Per-agent hook install/check: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/<name>/hooks.go`\n- Settings schema: `EntireSettings.Review map[string][]string` in `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Checkpoint fields: `Kind`, `ReviewSkills` on `CommittedMetadata`; `HasReview` on `CheckpointSummary` — both in `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/`\n\n## Settings example\n\n```json\n{\n  \"review\": {\n    \"claude-code\": [\"/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr\", \"/test-auditor\"],\n    \"codex\": [\"/codex:adversarial-review\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nKeys are registry agent names. Values are skill invocations passed verbatim to the agent in the composed initial prompt."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":206141,"output_tokens":2188,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":579,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2188,"cache_read_input_tokens":206141,"cache_creation_input_tokens":579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":579},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaJcb9Yoh2jL5gX4LTmFW","type":"assistant","uuid":"88196071-eee2-4428-8d32-7dd241650a6d","timestamp":"2026-04-22T10:00:33.759Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/