{"parentUuid":"875cbe3a-3911-400c-aa49-981a59bc40e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HpSTtkdhWQquT3DzRMBv9k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Because `entire review` and the agent's session hooks are **different processes** that don't share state.\n\nThe handoff problem:\n\n- **`entire review`** knows the answer to *what* (agent, skills, worktree) but not *where* (the session ID doesn't exist yet — the agent hasn't started).\n- **The session hook** (fired later, as a fresh `entire hooks <agent> user-prompt-submit` subprocess invoked by the agent) knows *where* (it has the session ID) but not *what* (it has no idea whether this session is a review).\n\nThey need to meet somewhere. The marker is that meeting point — a tiny file on disk written by the former, read by the latter.\n\n## Why not the obvious alternatives\n\n**Environment variable.** You'd set `ENTIRE_REVIEW=1` when spawning the agent. But the agent's hook is invoked as a *separate* process spawned by the agent itself — not a child of `entire review`. Whether your env var reaches that grandchild depends on the agent's internal plumbing, and some agents (cursor, opencode via JSON hook configs) don't pass environment through at all. Not portable across agents.\n\n**Agent-specific CLI flags.** You could pass `--review-mode` when launching Claude Code, and the agent could tell its hooks. But this requires per-agent cooperation, breaks for non-launchable agents (where the user starts the agent manually), and doesn't exist as a contract in any of the agent CLIs.\n\n**Use the session ID.** `entire review` doesn't know it yet — the session is created when the agent starts, *after* the command has returned.\n\n**Check session state after the fact.** You'd have to scan newly-created sessions and retroactively tag one as a review. But which one? Concurrent sessions in the same directory make this ambiguous, and you'd tag the wrong session if the user opened a non-review Claude window between `entire review` and their real review session.\n\n**Commit trailer.** Nothing has been committed yet.\n\n## What the marker actually solves\n\n1. **Cross-process state** with a trivially reliable medium (one small JSON file, `.git/entire-sessions/` is already the state directory used by the rest of the strategy).\n2. **Late binding**: the review intent is declared before the session exists, and gets applied to *whichever* session starts next in that worktree.\n3. **Worktree scoping**: `WorktreePath` on the marker is the mechanism that prevents a non-review session in worktree B from claiming a marker written for worktree A.\n4. **Self-cleanup**: adoption deletes the marker, so leftover state from a crashed command doesn't silently tag a future unrelated session.\n\nIt's the minimum-viable handoff — smaller than you could do with any of the alternatives, and agnostic to which agent you're using."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":866,"cache_read_input_tokens":208951,"output_tokens":1597,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1597,"cache_read_input_tokens":208951,"cache_creation_input_tokens":866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":866},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaJd1umHWK8jCcnuZMiBm","type":"assistant","uuid":"b7d8cda8-02cd-424f-b944-2dea99c8b9f1","timestamp":"2026-04-22T10:05:57.819Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
