{"parentUuid":"2db8a025-1ca2-4273-973d-ca81dfb649ef","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5c727b84-d807-426b-9266-513235ef9203","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"I wonder if it makes more sense to rather attach the session as review if you want to do a review manually then do `--track-only` and then make sure you run the session right after..."},"uuid":"eaa6a37f-3a15-4411-bae1-dfc45e4e38e5","timestamp":"2026-04-22T10:07:11.935Z","permissionMode":"acceptEdits","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
{"parentUuid":"eaa6a37f-3a15-4411-bae1-dfc45e4e38e5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HnwSFVeQUXudBVHHm8XQFM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_read_input_tokens":209817,"output_tokens":2809,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1652,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2809,"cache_read_input_tokens":209817,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1652},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaJd9WtqVhGqWhMs7K7pW","type":"assistant","uuid":"7e043b63-cd74-495f-b6f4-3b6092f6c303","timestamp":"2026-04-22T10:07:49.949Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
{"parentUuid":"7e043b63-cd74-495f-b6f4-3b6092f6c303","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HnwSFVeQUXudBVHHm8XQFM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reasonable design — and honestly probably better for the manual case. The current `--track-only` has an awkward property: it sits in a state where \"the next session in this worktree becomes a review\", which creates a small footgun window. If you write the marker and then accidentally open an unrelated Claude window before your intended review session, that unrelated session eats the marker.\n\nAn `entire review --attach` flow would invert that: do the review in whatever session you want, then tag it explicitly by session ID. No race, no sitting state, no \"did my marker get claimed by the wrong session?\" worry.\n\n## The main tradeoffs\n\n**Skills list.** The marker carries `Skills` into the adoption step, which ends up in `CommittedMetadata.ReviewSkills`. An attach flow needs to source that somewhere — options are (a) a `--skills` flag, (b) read from saved config, or (c) drop the skills record and just tag `Kind=agent_review`. (c) is tempting but loses the audit trail (\"which skills actually ran?\"). (b) is the most ergonomic but only works if the user stuck to configured skills.\n\n**Timing window.** Attach must happen before the PostCommit hook condenses the session. Condensation is triggered by `git commit`; a session that's been committed has its metadata frozen on `entire/checkpoints/v1`. Mutating a condensed session means rebuilding the checkpoint tree and writing a new commit on that branch — doable but an order of magnitude more code than mutating session state.\n\n**Session disambiguation.** \"Attach to which session?\" — most-recent-active in current worktree is the obvious answer, but concurrent sessions make this a real question. The marker design sidesteps it because it's the session that *claims* the marker, not the command that *picks* the session.\n\n**Lost signal.** Pre-declaration is a small commitment device — \"I'm about to review\" vs. \"I already reviewed, trust me.\" Not a strong argument against attach; the condensed metadata is the source of truth either way.\n\n## My take\n\nKeep spawn-with-marker as the default (the `entire review` with no flags path) — it works cleanly when `entire review` launches the agent, and the hook adoption is unambiguous. \n\nDrop `--track-only`, add `--attach` for the manual case. The attach flow needs one decision: whether to require `--skills` or default to the configured skills for the selected agent. I'd start with \"read from configured skills, error if none configured, allow `--skills` override\" — keeps UX consistent with the spawn flow.\n\nWant me to sketch what that code change would look like, or leave it as design conversation for now?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_read_input_tokens":209817,"output_tokens":2809,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1652,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2809,"cache_read_input_tokens":209817,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1652},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaJd9WtqVhGqWhMs7K7pW","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6f546d3-4db3-48b8-83ee-cea706df5e84","timestamp":"2026-04-22T10:08:03.341Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
