{"parentUuid":"b74595b2-3382-4de0-97cc-00285a2ec40c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014bdsiarAiYx7p4P1htw9RL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That maps cleanly. `entire attach` already takes a `<session-id>` and does most of the heavy lifting: finds the session state, reads the transcript, creates a checkpoint, links it to HEAD via the `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. The path I'd take is extending that existing command with a `--review` flag rather than inventing a parallel one — the attach flow already has a `WriteCommittedOptions` struct populated for `checkpoint.WriteCommitted`, which is the exact place `Kind` and `ReviewSkills` get set.\n\n## Shape\n\n```\nentire attach <session-id>             # existing\nentire attach <session-id> --review    # new: also tag as agent_review\n```\n\nImplementation is small:\n\n1. Add a `--review` bool flag (and optionally `--skills` for the skills list; default to the configured skills for the resolved agent, error if none).\n2. In `runAttach`, when the flag is set, pass `Kind: session.KindAgentReview` and `ReviewSkills: skills` into the `WriteCommittedOptions` passed to `checkpoint.WriteCommitted`. The summary's `HasReview = true` derivation already falls out of the existing `state.Kind.IsReview()` seam.\n3. For the already-checkpointed branch (line 102 in attach.go — \"session already has a checkpoint, just offer to link it\"), either re-condense with the review fields set, or flip `HasReview` on the existing summary. The second is minimal; the first is more principled.\n\n## What this lets `entire review` become\n\nWith `attach --review` in place, `entire review` shrinks back to just the spawn path:\n\n- Default: launch configured agent with the review prompt, marker-based adoption (unchanged — it's the clean path).\n- `--edit`: reopen the picker.\n- *Drop `--track-only`*, point users at `attach --review` instead.\n- Drop the launcher-fallback `--track-on