{"parentUuid":"cb567dc9-714c-436e-9c13-be582be12239","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01G6oQzpTuzTXAEraqBE2HVm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I like it — `skills` is a leaky abstraction. It assumes a review is a list of slash commands, but really what we want to record is \"what the reviewer actually asked.\" That's the composed prompt for spawn, and the first user prompt for attach. One concept, two sources.\n\n## What would change\n\n**Storage.** `ReviewSkills []string` → `ReviewPrompt string` on:\n- `session.State`\n- `checkpoint.WriteCommittedOptions` + `CommittedMetadata`\n- `PendingReviewMarker`\n- JSON field `\"review_skills\"` → `\"review_prompt\"` (no back-compat concern — feature is unreleased)\n\n**Settings.** `review: map[string][]string` → `review: map[string]string`. Per agent, one string. Simple case stays trivial (`\"claude-code\": \"/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr\"`), complex case works (`\"claude-code\": \"Please review and run /test-auditor, then /silent-failure-hunter\"`).\n\n**Picker.** Still offers curated skills, but writes them joined into a prompt string — e.g. user selects `/review-pr` + `/test-auditor`, saved as `\"Please run these review skills in order:\\n1. /review-pr\\n2. /test-auditor\"`. Gives users a good default they can then edit freely. Losing the structured list in settings makes multi-line manual editing trickier, which is the real UX cost.\n\n**Spawn path.** `composeReviewPrompt([]string)` goes away; the prompt is already the prompt. `runReview` just passes `review[agentName]` straight to `launcher.LaunchCmd(ctx, prompt)` and stores it on the marker.\n\n**Attach path.** Pulls the session's first user prompt from the transcript (we already parse transcripts in attach — `ag.ReadTranscript` + there's existing prompt extraction for `meta.FirstPrompt` at `attach.go:147`). Stores that as `ReviewPrompt`.\n\n## The real tradeoff\n\nYou gain flexibility (prompts can express workflow, not just command lists) and unified semantics (spawn and attach record the same shape). You lose structured queryability — today `review_skills: [\"/a\", \"/b\"]` is grep-friendly for \"which reviews ran `/test-auditor`?\" With prompts, that becomes substring match. For audit/reporting purposes, that's a real regression, though one you might not care about yet.\n\nIf you want the best of both, you could keep `ReviewSkills` as a derived/parsed field alongside `ReviewPrompt` — extract `/slash-prefixed` tokens from the prompt at write time. But that's the kind of half-measure that usually ages badly.\n\nI'd ship just `ReviewPrompt` and accept the queryability loss. Want me to fold this into the attach work — rename `ReviewSkills` → `ReviewPrompt` across the codebase, collapse the picker output into a string, and have `entire review attach` use `meta.FirstPrompt`?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2142,"cache_read_input_tokens":223613,"output_tokens":2650,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2142,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2650,"cache_read_input_tokens":223613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2142,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2142},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaJepszoKnmqCFSSUdCDy","type":"assistant","uuid":"4f0eef97-14e9-41f8-bc84-72819331764f","timestamp":"2026-04-22T10:29:58.624Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
