\t},\n140\t\t\"codex\": {\n141\t\t\t{Name: \"/codex:review\", Desc: \"Codex review\"},\n142\t\t\t{Name: \"/codex:adversarial-review\", Desc: \"Adversarial review — red-team\"},\n143\t\t},\n144\t}\n145\t\n146\t// sameWorktreePath compares two worktree paths after filepath.Clean. Both\n147\t// paths come from paths.WorktreeRoot, so an exact-bytes match is expected in\n148\t// the common case; Clean is defense-in-depth against trailing slashes and\n149\t// duplicate separators.\n150\tfunc sameWorktreePath(a, b string) bool {\n151\t\treturn filepath.Clean(a) == filepath.Clean(b)\n152\t}\n153\t\n154\t// adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto reads any pending review marker and applies it\n155\t// to the given session state. Returns (newState, modified, error). If the\n156\t// state already has Kind set (e.g., a subsequent turn of a review session),\n157\t// the marker is left in place and modified=false — adoption only happens on\n158\t// first tag. The marker is cleared on successful first adoption.\n159\t//\n160\t// Scoping rules — the marker is left untouched (not cleared) when a scope\n161\t// mismatch still leaves open the possibility that a future session could\n162\t// legitimately claim it:\n163\t//\n164\t//   - WorktreePath: a Claude session in worktree A must not claim a marker\n165\t//     meant for a session `entire review` spawned in worktree B. Both\n166\t//     worktrees share the same .git/entire-sessions/ directory.\n167\t//   - AgentName: a cursor session must not claim a marker that records a\n168\t//     claude-code review — the review config and skills are agent-specific,\n169\t//     and whichever session fires its UserPromptSubmit hook first would\n170\t//     otherwise silently steal the wrong agent's review metadata.\n171\t//\n172\t// StartingSHA is different: once HEAD moves past the marker's commit, no\n173\t// future session will meaningfully match the original review intent.\n174\t// A stale marker is cleared rather than left to mis-tag a later unrelat