{"parentUuid":"fba4df9c-7708-4282-8b8f-0e826f5f8217","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01N2BVAuhbxMRm4uc6JqKmDG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The skill list comes from three sources that converge on a single storage shape.\n\n## Storage\n\nOne place: `.entire/settings.json`, the `review` field, typed as `map[string][]string`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"review\": {\n    \"claude-code\": [\"/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr\", \"/test-auditor\"],\n    \"codex\": [\"/codex:adversarial-review\"],\n    \"my-external-agent\": [\"/custom-review\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nKey = agent name (registry key like `claude-code`, `codex`, `gemini`, external agent name). Value = list of skill invocations, passed verbatim to the agent.\n\n## Three sources feed that map\n\n**1. First-run picker** (`runReviewConfigPicker` in `review.go:214`). On first `entire review` or `entire review --edit`, presents a `huh` multi-select per installed agent. The picker only offers:\n\n- Agents whose hooks are installed (`GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled`).\n- Agents listed in `curatedReviewSkills` — a **hardcoded map** in `review.go:131`:\n\n  ```go\n  var curatedReviewSkills = map[string][]curatedSkill{\n      \"claude-code\": {\n          {Name: \"/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr\", Desc: \"Full PR review\"},\n          {Name: \"/pr-review-toolkit:code-reviewer\", Desc: \"Code review for standards\"},\n          {Name: \"/test-auditor\", Desc: \"Test coverage audit\"},\n          // ... 3 more\n      },\n      \"codex\": {\n          {Name: \"/codex:review\", Desc: \"Codex review\"},\n          {Name: \"/codex:adversarial-review\", Desc: \"Adversarial review — red-team\"},\n      },\n  }\n  ```\n\n  External agents and uncurated agents (gemini, cursor, opencode, copilot-cli, factoryai-droid) aren't offered here.\n\n**2. Manual settings.json edit.** Users edit the file directly to add entries for agents the picker doesn't surface, or to use skills outside the curated list. The last simplify round added `mergePickerResults` so running `--edit` doesn't clobber these manual entries.\n\n**3. `--skills` flag on attach** (`resolveReviewSkills` in `attach.go:108`). On `entire attach --review` / `entire review attach`, the `--skills \"/a,/b\"` flag can override the settings lookup for a one-shot attach. Only affects that single invocation; nothing is written back to settings.\n\n## How each command consumes the list\n\n**`entire review` (spawn)** at `review.go:499`:\n1. Read `s.Review[agentName]` from settings.\n2. Call `selectReviewAgent(s.Review, --agent override)` to pick the agent.\n3. Compose the skills list into a prompt via `composeReviewPrompt`:\n   ```\n   Please run these review skills in order:\n     1. /skill-a\n     2. /skill-b\n   ```\n4. Store both on the marker (`Skills` + composed `Prompt`).\n5. Agent adopts marker → both copied into `session.State.ReviewSkills` + `ReviewPrompt`.\n6. On commit → condensed into `CommittedMetadata.ReviewSkills` + `ReviewPrompt`.\n\n**`entire attach --review <id>` (post-hoc)** at `attach.go:197`:\n1. Detect the real agent via transcript auto-detect.\n2. Call `resolveReviewSkills(ctx, ag.Name(), flagSkills)`:\n   - If `--skills` given, use that.\n   - Else `s.ReviewSkillsFor(ag.Name())` — read from settings.\n   - Else error with \"run `entire review --edit`\".\n3. Store on session state + checkpoint metadata.\n4. `ReviewPrompt` comes from `meta.FirstPrompt` (the session's first user prompt from the transcript).\n\n## What's stored in the checkpoint\n\nTwo fields on `CommittedMetadata` (and `session.State`):\n\n- **`ReviewSkills []string`** — the structured list. Queryable for \"did any review include /test-auditor?\"\n- **`ReviewPrompt string`** — the ground-truth text the agent received (composed-skills for spawn, first-user-prompt for attach). Primary source of truth.\n\n## Where to add a new skill\n\n- **For a curated agent (claude-code, codex)**: edit `curatedReviewSkills` in `review.go`. New users get the option in the picker.\n- **For any agent, ad hoc**: edit `.entire/settings.json` directly. `mergePickerResults` preserves your entry across `--edit` runs.\n- **For a one-off attach**: `entire attach --review --skills \"/your-skill\" <session-id>`.\n\n## Known limitation\n\nThe picker is binary: curated skills only, no free-text entry. If you want custom skills for claude-code (e.g., your team's own `/internal-review`), you either edit settings.json or pass `--skills` on attach. Adding a free-text option to the picker is the natural next step, but hasn't been done."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":443639,"output_tokens":2598,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":442,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2598,"cache_read_input_tokens":443639,"cache_creation_input_tokens":442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":442},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaJxrRqbQNv5NWEHsfEzp","type":"assistant","uuid":"9f2192f2-a708-4104-8c20-2047f1b8e3c1","timestamp":"2026-04-22T14:26:21.955Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
