{"parentUuid":"fd241f64-ba8e-48d4-883d-4cd5ef75be88","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017FwfLp2xeyysFnGqTwuww5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two separate issues — quick answers:\n\n## 1. The picker should signpost \"initial setup\"\n\nValid UX gap. Right now `runReview` at `review.go:499` silently drops into the picker when `s.Review` is empty. The header \"Configuring review skills for 2 agent(s)\" tells you what's happening only after you're already in it. Minimal fix: print a one-line banner + a press-enter confirmation before the picker when it's the first-run path, and a one-line afterword like \"Review config saved. Now running review...\" so the auto-transition to the actual review is explicit.\n\nSomething like:\n\n```\nNo review config found — let's set one up.\nPick the skills you want to run on each agent. Saved to\n.entire/settings.json; edit later with `entire review --edit`.\n\nPress enter to continue, Ctrl-C to cancel.\n```\n\nAlternative (stricter): error out with \"No review config. Run `entire review --edit` first.\" — but that's a step backwards for first-run ergonomics. I'd prefer the banner.\n\n## 2. Querying skills\n\nThere's no built-in skill query today. The picker's list is the hardcoded `curatedReviewSkills` map in `review.go:131`; it doesn't ask the agent what's installed.\n\nThe realistic options, in order of cost:\n\n- **Print the curated list.** Trivial — add `entire review --list-skills` that prints `curatedReviewSkills`. Doesn't reflect what's actually available on the user's machine.\n- **Scan the agent's skills directory.** For Claude Code specifically, skills live as markdown files under `~/.claude/skills/` and `.claude/skills/`. A `Discover()` method per agent could glob that and return `[]string`. Would make the picker reflect reality for users who've installed custom skills, but every agent implements skills differently (Codex has `/codex:*`, Cursor doesn't have them at all), so each agent would need its own discovery logic.\n- **Accept free-text in the picker.** Let users type skill names alongside the curated list. Loosens the picker from being \"pick from this hardcoded menu\" to \"pick some and type others.\" Solves the custom-skill gap without discovery.\n- **Full shell-out to the agent.** `claude --list-skills` or equivalent. Most agents don't have such a flag today, and depending on it is fragile.\n\nMy instinct: scanning `~/.claude/skills/` for claude-code would be the highest-value addition, and free-text in the picker would cover every other agent. But neither is trivial — especially the per-agent abstraction for discovery.\n\nWant me to implement the banner fix now, and sketch out the skill-discovery options as a separate design pass? Or dive into one of them?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2952,"cache_read_input_tokens":444081,"output_tokens":2346,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2952,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2346,"cache_read_input_tokens":444081,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2952,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2952},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaJxxRqkqno376Es9j65N","type":"assistant","uuid":"8413c066-1c3b-4625-ba91-6338de5f067c","timestamp":"2026-04-22T14:27:37.932Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
