{"parentUuid":"35a10c8d-cf6c-4a9e-a07c-f7e4d8065e00","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JntkZvcGQCJeH4Dgdz5mu8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — Codex uses the same layout as Claude Code. Both store skills as:\n\n```\n~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md          # Claude Code: user skills\n~/.codex/skills/<name>/SKILL.md           # Codex: user skills\n~/.codex/skills/.system/<name>/SKILL.md   # Codex: system skills\n```\n\nEach `SKILL.md` has YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description` — directly mappable to the `curatedSkill{Name, Desc}` the picker already uses.\n\nOn your machine, `~/.codex/skills/` already exists (empty user dir, with `.system` holding Codex's built-ins like `skill-creator`). So the discovery shape is literally identical for both agents — walk the directory tree, find every `SKILL.md`, parse its frontmatter.\n\n## One subtlety: invocation naming\n\nSkills can nest, and the invocation name depends on the structure:\n\n| Filesystem layout | Invocation |\n|---|---|\n| `skills/test-auditor/SKILL.md` | `/test-auditor` |\n| `skills/gstack/ship/SKILL.md` | `/gstack:ship` |\n| `skills/gstack/SKILL.md` (has children) | `/gstack` (the plugin itself) |\n\nCodex additionally seems to namespace with a `/codex:` prefix in some contexts (based on the current curated list: `/codex:review`, `/codex:adversarial-review`). I'm not 100% sure whether that prefix is always required or just for system skills — worth verifying against a real Codex invocation before building this in.\n\n## Shape of the change\n\nExtract a small interface both agents can implement:\n\n```go\ntype SkillProvider interface {\n    DiscoverSkills(ctx context.Context) ([]curatedSkill, error)\n}\n```\n\nImplementation:\n\n1. A shared `skillsdir` package that walks a directory, parses SKILL.md frontmatter, and returns `(name, description)` pairs + a relative path.\n2. `claudecode` and `codex` implement `DiscoverSkills()` by calling the shared helper on their respective home dirs (`$CLAUDE_HOME|~/.claude` and `$CODEX_HOME|~/.codex`), plus the project-level `.claude/skills` / `.codex/skills`.\n3. Each agent converts the relative path into an invocation string using its own naming rules.\n4. The picker calls `DiscoverSkills()` first, then unions with the hardcoded curated list (or replaces it entirely — arguable).\n\n## Tradeoffs\n\n- **Pro**: reflects reality — users see what they actually have installed. Picks up plugins shipped via `/plugin` commands or manually cloned.\n- **Con**: brittle to layout changes (either agent could restructure their skills dir). The SKILL.md frontmatter format is also not formally specified — both agents use it but could diverge.\n- **Middle ground**: keep the curated list as a fallback. Merge discovered + curated, dedup by name. New users without any skills installed still see something.\n\nWant me to build this — shared `skillsdir` helper + `DiscoverSkills` on both claudecode and codex + picker integration — as a new commit chain? If so, any preference on whether project-level `.claude/skills`/`.codex/skills` should also be scanned, or just the home dir?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_read_input_tokens":453500,"output_tokens":2686,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":566,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2686,"cache_read_input_tokens":453500,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":566},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaJyBT33zGtHW6iDWCYUj","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c42c0d3-9d7f-40c1-9515-495250f0085c","timestamp":"2026-04-22T14:30:34.841Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"