{"parentUuid":"d7801bc0-7d24-4c8c-adec-1403cd81f24f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Wo53eQYxt6VDb8yDH14kT7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed as `b05ffb18c`.\n\n## What changed\n\nAdded `refreshForExistingCheckpoint` to `attach.go`. When HEAD's trailer references an existing checkpoint, it runs resume's `getMetadataTree` for its side effects:\n\n1. **Checkpoint-remote fetch** (if configured)\n2. **Treeless fetch from origin**\n3. **Local branch** (no-op if already present)\n4. **Full fetch from origin**\n5. **Remote-tracking ref** (`origin/entire/checkpoints/v1`)\n\nReturns a freshly-opened repo handle (so go-git's packfile cache sees any fetched objects), which replaces `repo` downstream. Then the existing guard and `WriteCommitted` both operate on the fresh state — so:\n\n- The review-attach conflict guard catches sessionID collisions that exist on remote-only.\n- `findSessionIndex`'s \"next available\" picks the correct index when appending a new session, avoiding push-time clobbers.\n\nNon-fatal on fetch failure — logs at warn and proceeds with local state. Better than blocking attach on transient network errors.\n\n## Scope / limitations\n\n- **V1 only.** `getMetadataTree` covers v1. V2 has a separate `getV2MetadataTree` with the same pattern — if users run in v2-only mode, the same bug could recur there. Straightforward follow-up if it matters.\n- **No new integration test for the remote-only scenario.** Would need multi-repo setup; the unit test `TestAttach_ReviewWithExistingCheckpointErrorsEvenWithoutSessionState` still covers the local-visibility case. The refresh path is covered by resume's existing test surface.\n- **Extracted into a helper** to keep `runAttach` under the `maintidx` lint threshold (score was 19, threshold ~20).\n\nFull `mise run test:ci` green."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_in