{"parentUuid":"6481df0e-545f-4e30-8301-031b797f8f2b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XTdK5tC3P5ZKSZjbsBppwZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the full picture. Here's how the picker builds its skill list today:\n\n## Two sources, merged per agent\n\n**1. Curated built-ins** — hardcoded in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/skilldiscovery/registry.go:28`:\n\n```go\nvar curatedBuiltins = map[string][]CuratedSkill{\n    \"claude-code\": {\n        {Name: \"/review\",          Desc: \"Review changes and find issues\"},\n        {Name: \"/security-review\", Desc: \"Scan git diff for security issues\"},\n        {Name: \"/simplify\",        Desc: \"Review recent changes for code quality\"},\n    },\n    \"codex\":      {{Name: \"/review\", Desc: \"Review current changes and find issues\"}},\n    \"gemini-cli\": {},\n}\n```\n\nThese are review-adjacent commands that ship with the agent binary — no plugin install needed. The picker reads them via `CuratedBuiltinsFor(agentName)` at `review.go:332`.\n\n**2. Disk-scanned plugin skills** — via the `agent.SkillDiscoverer` interface (`review.go:335-343`). Each agent implements `DiscoverReviewSkills(ctx)` differently:\n\n- **Claude Code** (`agent/claudecode/discovery.go`) walks four locations:\n  - `~/.claude/plugins/cache/<marketplace>/<plugin>/<version>/{skills,commands,agents}/`\n  - `~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (user-level skills)\n  - `~/.claude/commands/*.md` (user-level commands)\n  - `~/.claude/agents/*.md` (user-level agents)\n  \n  Each SKILL.md's YAML frontmatter is parsed for `name:` and `description:`. Invocation is `/plugin:skill` for plugin-scoped entries, `/skill` for bare ones.\n\n- **Codex** (`agent/codex/discovery.go`) — similar shape for `~/.codex/skills/`.\n\n- **Gemini CLI** (`agent/geminicli/discovery.go`) — also filesystem-based.\n\n**Filter**: every discovered entry runs through `skilldiscovery.Matches(name, description)` at `match.go:35`. Only invocations whose **name** contains a review-adjacent keyword pass: `review`, `audit`, `inspect`, `critique`, `assess`, `security-scan`. Descriptions are ignored on purpose (noisy). That's how `/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr` survives (has \"review\" in the plugin prefix) while `/lint` doesn't.\n\n**Dedupe**: `filterOutBuiltinCollisions(discovered, builtinNames)` at `review.go:345` removes any discovered skill whose name matches a curated built-in — so a curated `/review` doesn't appear twice when it's also on disk.\n\n## Install hints\n\nFor plugins we know are common but aren't installed, the picker shows passive \"install more\" messages (`skilldiscovery/registry.go:45`). `ActiveInstallHintsFor(agentName, discoveredSet)` suppresses hints whose `ProvidesAny` skill names are already in the discovered set — so if `/pr-review-toolkit:review-pr` is discovered, the \"install pr-review-toolkit\" hint disappears.\n\n## Preselection (after your last bug report)\n\nPreviously-saved skills are partitioned by `splitSavedPicks(saved, curated, discovered)` into the two buckets the picker renders. Each bucket feeds both:\n- The `huh.MultiSelect.Value()` binding (so the saved list is the starting state).\n- `.Selected(true)` on matching options (so the UI renders them checked).\n\nSkills in the saved list that match neither bucket (external-agent entries, plugins uninstalled since last edit) don't show in the picker — but `mergePickerResults` preserves them on save for agents the picker didn't surface.\n\n## What this means for extensibility\n\n- **Adding a curated built-in for an existing agent**: edit `curatedBuiltins` in `registry.go:28`.\n- **Adding a new agent to the picker**: implement `SkillDiscoverer` on the agent + add an entry in `curatedBuiltins` and/or `installHints`. Also must be in `IsEligible(agentName)` returning true.\n- **Changing what counts as \"review-adjacent\"**: edit `reviewKeywords` in `match.go:11`.\n\nThe hardcoded `curatedBuiltins` / `installHints` maps are the main extension seam — everything else (discovery walk, dedupe, match filter) is agent-generic."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":942,"cache_read_input_tokens":705824,"output_tokens":1542,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":942,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1542,"cache_read_input_tokens":705824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":942,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":942},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLgdg9bRJzGvpEcz9SbM","type":"assistant","uuid":"0ffd5522-7c3a-47cf-9cd2-94874d44af93","timestamp":"2026-04-23T12:14:34.827Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
