{"parentUuid":"b363384d-2def-4fcf-959c-81f9d221711f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FXSre8vNYqL1aw5YeM6Wng","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the full inventory organized by what each test defends against, specifically around the review-attach overwrite issue and the broader review flow.\n\n## The overwrite bug — direct defenses\n\n**`TestAttach_ReviewAppendsAsAdditionalSessionWhenIDDiffers`** (`attach_test.go:776`) — the closest test to the reported bug. First attach creates a checkpoint with session A at index 0. Second attach with a *different* session ID in review mode must land at index 1, with both sessions preserved on the summary. Asserts the exact shape that was violated in the production report. **Passes** — the static append logic is correct.\n\n**`TestAttach_ReviewWithExistingCheckpointErrors`** (`attach_test.go:740`) — the re-attach case: same session ID, already condensed into a checkpoint. Review-tagging it again must error instead of overwriting. Relies on the session state's `LastCheckpointID` being set.\n\n**`TestAttach_ReviewWithExistingCheckpointErrorsEvenWithoutSessionState`** (`attach_test.go:868`) — gap closure for the above. Simulates the case where session state is missing/deleted (so `LastCheckpointID` doesn't catch it), but the on-disk checkpoint still has that session. Uses `ReadSessionContentByID` to detect the sessionID is already there and refuses. This is the guard I added after your first overwrite report.\n\n**Runtime tripwire** (not a test, but a log-based detector in `writeStandardCheckpointEntries`) — fires a `WARN checkpoint write overwrites session 0 with a different sessionID` if the writer ever lands at index 0 while that slot already has a different session's metadata. This is the safety net for whatever edge case we couldn't reproduce.\n\n## Marker adoption (spawn path, `lifecycle_test.go`)\n\nThese cover the `entire review` spawn flow — marker written by the CLI, adopted by the agent's first hook call:\n\n- **`TestAdoptPendingReviewMarker`** — happy path: marker exists, session adopts, Kind/ReviewSkills/ReviewPrompt all populated, marker cleared.\n- **`TestAdoptPendingReviewMarker_NoMarker`** — no marker on disk → no-op, session unchanged.\n- **`TestAdoptPendingReviewMarker_AlreadyReview`** — subsequent turns of an already-tagged session don't re-apply the marker (marker stays in place for cleanup later).\n- **`TestAdoptPendingReviewMarker_OtherWorktreeLeavesMarker`** — worktree scoping: session in worktree B doesn't steal a marker meant for worktree A. Marker survives.\n- **`TestAdoptPendingReviewMarker_DifferentAgentLeavesMarker`** — agent scoping: cursor session doesn't steal a claude-code marker. Marker survives.\n- **`TestAdoptPendingReviewMarker_StaleSHAClearsMarker`** — HEAD drift: marker written at SHA A, HEAD moved to SHA B before adoption → marker cleared, session not tagged. Prevents ghost reviews.\n\n## Review command plumbing (`review_test.go`)\n\n- **`TestRunReview_MissingHooksAborts`** — hooks-installed gate fires before marker write.\n- **`TestRunReview_NonLaunchableAgentPreservesMarker`** — agents without `LaunchCmd` (cursor/opencode/etc.) fall back to persist-marker mode; marker survives for manual launch.\n- **`TestRunReview_MissingConfiguredSkillAbortsBeforeMarker`** — configured skill not installed (built-in or discovered) → abort before writing marker.\n- **`TestRunReview_PromptOnlyConfigSkipsVerification`** — custom prompt without `skills` list → skills-verification gate skipped.\n- **`TestComposeReviewPrompt_SkillsOnly` / `_CustomPromptWinsOverSkills` / `_EmptyConfigReturnsEmpty`** — prompt composition precedence (user's custom prompt beats the default \"run these in order\" template; empty config returns \"\").\n- **`TestSelectReviewAgent_OverrideResolvesSpecificAgent`** — `--agent` flag resolves a non-default configured agent; unknown override surfaces a helpful error listing configured agents.\n- **`TestKindIsReview`** — `session.Kind.IsReview()` returns true only for review kinds.\n\n## Attach surfaces (`attach_test.go`)\n\n- **`TestAttach_WithReviewFlag`** — `--review` flag sets session state's `Kind = agent_review` + propagates to checkpoint metadata.\n- **`REDACTED`** — attach must *not* silently pull skills from `settings.Review[agent]`; only `--skills` counts as a user claim. Prevents leaking spawn-config into post-hoc attach.\n- **`TestReviewAttachCmd_TagsSession`** — `entire review attach <id>` subcommand ends up in the same code path as `entire attach --review <id>`.\n- **`TestAttachCmd_ReviewWithoutSkillsOrConfigSucceeds`** — review-attach with no skills is valid (`ReviewPrompt` is the source of truth, `ReviewSkills` is a queryable convenience).\n- **`TestAttachCmd_ReviewAutoDetectsAgent`** — spawn-path agent auto-detection works for review-attach too (sessionID→transcript→agent, with no `--agent` flag).\n\n## Integration tests (`integration_test/review_test.go`)\n\nThese drive the binary against a real repo with hooks simulation:\n\n- **`TestReview_MarkerAdoptionCondensesReviewMetadataOnNextCommit`** — end-to-end: marker written → hook adopts → next commit condenses → `HasReview=true` + metadata fields propagate to `entire/checkpoints/v1`.\n- **`TestReviewAttach_TagsAttachedSessionAsReview`** — `entire review attach` via the CLI binary, checkpoint metadata has `Kind=agent_review` + skills.\n- **`TestReview_MarkerAdoption_WrongAgentDoesNotAdoptMarker`** — marker for claude-code; gemini session fires hook first; claude-code session then adopts. Agent scoping end-to-end.\n- **`TestReview_MarkerAdoption_StaleMarkerIsIgnoredAfterHeadMoves`** — commit moves HEAD; session starts after; marker discarded.\n- **`TestReview_MissingSkillAtSpawn_ErrorsCleanly`** — misconfigured skill fails gracefully with a user-facing error (no marker written).\n\n## What we *don't* have\n\nThe gap: there's no test that reproduces the exact overwrite you saw, because I couldn't trigger it on a minimal setup. The closest is `TestAttach_ReviewAppendsAsAdditionalSessionWhenIDDiffers`, which pins the expected append behavior — but it passes. So if the bug was a specific filesystem/timing interaction (fetch race, stale packfile handle, concurrent hook condensation), none of the unit/integration tests cover that.\n\nThe tripwire is our net for that — it doesn't prevent the bug, but it'll log loudly if it recurs, so we get a diagnostic breadcrumb instead of just the symptom.\n\nWant me to add an integration test that explicitly attempts the append-different-session scenario end-to-end via the binary? It wouldn't close the gap either (same reason — not reproducing), but it'd pin the binary-level behavior alongside the unit test."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":905214,"output_tokens":3547,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":344,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3547,"cache_read_input_tokens":905214,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":344},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLrjGz9QuYxGJ5bBohZw","type":"assistant","uuid":"b81a0818-bf49-4437-b0fa-9264d142b66d","timestamp":"2026-04-23T14:27:22.436Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
