{"parentUuid":"520e91f8-74b2-4861-a08e-90c8ae1929d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017MXoQyNPRY7JbqtcvF6bDf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The binding moment is `git commit`, not closing Claude. Timeline:\n\n## While Claude is running\n\n1. **`entire review`** writes the pending marker (agent, skills, composed prompt, starting SHA, worktree) to `.git/entire-sessions/review-pending.json`.\n2. **Claude starts**, fires `UserPromptSubmit` on its first turn.\n3. **Hook adopts the marker** (`adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto`) — tags the session state with `Kind = agent_review` + `ReviewSkills` + `ReviewPrompt`, clears the marker.\n4. **Session state lives at** `.git/entire-sessions/<session-id>.json` and now carries the review tag for the rest of its life.\n\n## When the condensation actually happens\n\n`lifecycle.go`'s phase state machine only condenses to `entire/checkpoints/v1` on **`GitCommit` events** — the `post-commit` hook. Not on session end.\n\nSo:\n\n- **If Claude makes commits during the session** (turn-start → edits → turn-end → commit → next turn...), each of those commits condenses the session state (including the review tag) into a fresh checkpoint. The commit gets an `Entire-Checkpoint: <id>` trailer. That checkpoint already has the review metadata.\n\n- **If Claude doesn't commit anything** during the session, closing Claude just transitions the session to `PhaseEnded`. The review tag stays in session state. Nothing lands on `entire/checkpoints/v1` yet.\n\n- **Your first commit after closing Claude** — whenever that happens, even days later — triggers the post-commit hook, which looks at ended sessions in this repo, sees one with `Kind = agent_review`, and condenses it. That commit's trailer links the review checkpoint.\n\n## Summary by scenario\n\n| What you did | When it lands on `entire/checkpoints/v1` |\n|---|---|\n| Claude made commits during the review | At each commit (already done by the time you close) |\n| Claude made no commits, you commit after closing | At that next `git commit` |\n| Claude made no commits, you never commit | Never — sits in session state, lost when state file is cleaned up |\n\n## Practical implication\n\nIf you run a review and Claude only *read* the repo (didn't commit anything), nothing is recorded on `entire/checkpoints/v1` until you commit. Amending the last commit with `git commit --amend --no-edit` (even with no staged changes) would trigger condensation via the same post-commit path.\n\nThe other way to guarantee recording without waiting for a commit is the post-hoc attach — `entire attach --review <session-id>` or `entire review attach <session-id>`. That writes the checkpoint directly and amends HEAD with the trailer."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":928200,"output_tokens":2722,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1007,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2722,"cache_read_input_tokens":928200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1007,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1007},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLuivYRkow6R2WrDYJqV","type":"assistant","uuid":"25fe522e-a260-4134-86c1-61c056474376","timestamp":"2026-04-23T15:06:28.914Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
