{"parentUuid":"bc0a71b7-6330-4343-a1e8-09e214ed853e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019g27LuS5wDJ8Yuvp72iMGt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fair point — reviews don't naturally produce commits. Right now the design forces a commit (or a manual `entire review attach`) to record the review, which is awkward.\n\nThe clean fix: `entire review` should auto-attach when Claude exits if no commit happened during the session. The CLI already knows:\n\n- The starting SHA (it's on the marker)\n- When Claude returns control\n\nSo after `launcher.Run()` returns, compare `currentHeadSHA` to the starting SHA. If unchanged → the session ran but nothing was condensed to `entire/checkpoints/v1`. Find the just-ended review session's state file (by worktree + `Kind=agent_review` + `started_at >= review-start-time`) and run the equivalent of `entire review attach <session-id>`. This amends HEAD with the trailer and writes the session to the metadata branch.\n\nIf HEAD did change (Claude made commits), those commits already condensed the session — nothing more needed.\n\n## Sketch\n\nIn `runReview`, after `execCmd.Run()`:\n\n```go\ncurrentHead, err := currentHeadSHA(ctx)\nif err == nil && currentHead == headSHA {\n    // Claude didn't commit. The review is only in session state;\n    // auto-attach so it lands on entire/checkpoints/v1 without the\n    // user needing a synthetic commit.\n    sessionID, findErr := findJustEndedReviewSession(ctx, worktreeRoot, startedAt)\n    if findErr == nil && sessionID != \"\" {\n        fmt.Fprintln(out, \"Recording review on the current commit...\")\n        if err := runAttach(ctx, out, sessionID, types.AgentName(agentName), attachOptions{\n            Force:        true,\n            Review:       true,\n            ReviewSkillsOverride: cfg.Skills,\n        }); err != nil {\n            fmt.Fprintf(out, \"Failed to auto-attach review: %v\\n\", err)\n            fmt.Fprintf(out, \"Run `entire review attach %s` manually to record.\\n\", sessionID)\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Tradeoffs\n\n- **Amends HEAD.** Review gets a trailer, which rewrites HEAD's SHA. If the user's branch is already pushed, this is a force-push situation. Maybe that's fine for a feature branch; not for main. We can detect \"HEAD is on a pushed branch\" and warn instead of silently amend — or just rely on the existing `--force` confirmation that `promptAmendCommit` already does.\n\n- **Finds the session to attach.** \"Last review session in this worktree started after review-start-time\" is the heuristic. Concurrent sessions in different tools are unlikely but possible; a more robust signal is \"session whose `ReviewPrompt` matches the one we wrote to the marker.\" That's deterministic.\n\n- **Skill propagation.** The review's skills are known (we composed them into the prompt). Pass them through `ReviewSkillsOverride` so the attach records them.\n\nMy recommendation: implement this with the ReviewPrompt-match heuristic (deterministic), and reuse `promptAmendCommit`'s existing confirmation path so the user sees what's happening.\n\nWant me to build it? Or is there a different shape you'd prefer (e.g., don't amend, write a parallel \"review-only\" record somewhere)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2747,"cache_read_input_tokens":929207,"output_tokens":3094,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2747,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3094,"cache_read_input_tokens":929207,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2747,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2747},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLutFj6EPrMMng9MpWcp","type":"assistant","uuid":"33644580-8c20-4c68-