{"parentUuid":"b8cdeac8-74f4-4a20-a138-271348ad1ac0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0114Bjxvn5rK9EjQuQkLnmiY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Right — amending to *add* a trailer changes HEAD's SHA, which is history rewriting. Amending to refresh a commit that *already has* the trailer is a no-op to the commit message itself (same trailer, same resulting content) — and `promptAmendCommit` at `attach.go:430` already detects this and skips the amend with a \"Commit X already has Entire-Checkpoint: Y\" message.\n\nSo the auto-attach rule becomes:\n\n- HEAD has a trailer → safe to auto-attach. `runAttach` adds the review session to the existing checkpoint, `promptAmendCommit` notices the trailer is already there and returns without touching the commit. No history rewrite.\n- HEAD has no trailer → auto-attach would force an amend. Don't do it silently. Tell the user what to do.\n\n## Proposed behavior\n\nAfter Claude exits, `entire review`:\n\n1. If `currentHead != startingHead` → a commit happened during the session, normal condensation already ran. Done.\n2. If `currentHead == startingHead`:\n   - If HEAD has a checkpoint trailer → auto-attach. The review session gets appended to the existing checkpoint. No commit modified.\n   - If HEAD has no trailer → print:\n\n     ```\n     Review session recorded in session state but not yet on entire/checkpoints/v1.\n     HEAD (abc1234) has no Entire-Checkpoint trailer, so recording would require\n     amending the commit. Choose one:\n\n       - Make a commit on this branch — the review will be attached automatically.\n       - Amend the current commit intentionally: entire review attach <session-id>\n     ```\n\n## Finding the session to attach\n\nThe `entire review` CLI wrote the marker with a known composed prompt + starting SHA. After Claude exits, scan session state files in this worktree where:\n\n- `Kind == agent_review`\n- `WorktreePath == <our worktree>`\n- `StartedAt >= <review command's start time>`\n- `ReviewPrompt == <the composed prompt we wrote to the marker>` (deterministic tiebreaker if multiple)\n\nMost of the time there's exactly one match. The prompt equality makes it robust against e.g. the user running two review CLIs concurrently.\n\n## One detail\n\nThe `runAttach` call would go through `verifyCheckpointLocallyAvailable` — which is fine, because HEAD's trailer points at a checkpoint that's in the local branch (it's the user's own recent work, or they pulled and the metadata came with it). If somehow the local checkpoint is still missing, the guard fires cleanly instead of silently creating one.\n\nWant me to build this? Or do you want to tune the \"no trailer → print message\" wording first?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3147,"cache_read_input_tokens":931954,"output_tokens":3967,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3147,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3967,"cache_read_input_tokens":931954,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3147},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLvqecXwUzoczkEut6CL","type":"assistant","uuid":"fcb4a986-bfad-4dbb-9bfc-7b0400f6832a","timestamp":"2026-04-23T15:21:40.080Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
