{"parentUuid":"8505ad46-5ada-43f9-90c2-9268a3a2cc92","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HUpNfHB539PzGTLFyg8HLQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — most of them apply to plain `entire attach` too. Here's the breakdown:\n\n## Apply to both plain attach and review-attach (gated only on `isExistingCheckpoint`)\n\n- **`refreshForExistingCheckpoint`** (`attach.go:222`) — runs the resume-style fetch chain whenever HEAD has a checkpoint trailer, regardless of `opts.Review`.\n- **`verifyCheckpointLocallyAvailable`** (`attach.go:227`) — the \"checkpoint referenced by HEAD is missing locally, refuse\" guard. Also fires for plain attach.\n\n## Apply globally (any checkpoint write, including hook-driven condensation)\n\n- **Session-count tripwire** in `writeStandardCheckpointEntries` — logs a `WARN` if a write lands at index 0 while entries already has a different session there. Fires on any path that writes to `entire/checkpoints/v1`, including the hook-driven condense path. Not specific to attach.\n\n## Apply to any attach (regardless of review)\n\n- **`defer logging.Close()` in `runAttach`** — flushes the buffered log writer on exit.\n\n## Review-only\n\n- **`opts.Review && isExistingCheckpoint` guard** at `attach.go:240` — the extra \"session already in checkpoint → error\" check. This is the one that's review-specific, because a plain attach of an already-recorded session just prints \"Session X already has checkpoint Y\" without erroring.\n\n## The net effect for `entire attach`\n\nIf your colleague's branch has commits with checkpoint trailers but the metadata branch wasn't fetched, then:\n\n- `entire attach <some-session-id>` **will now fetch** `entire/checkpoints/v1` via the resume-style chain.\n- If the fetch still doesn't bring the checkpoint in (colleague hasn't pushed the metadata, the checkpoint_remote is unreachable, etc.), the attach **will refuse** with the same `git fetch origin entire/checkpoints/v1:entire/checkpoints/v1` message — instead of silently creating a fresh one that would clobber the colleague's work on push.\n- If the write goes through and somehow ends up overwriting session 0 with a different ID, the tripwire logs a `WARN` to `.entire/logs/entire.log` — but now the attach path actually flushes that log.\n\nSo all the structural safety applies to plain attach. Only the review-attach-specific \"don't record a review twice\" guard is narrowed to review mode."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1431,"cache_read_input_tokens":939101,"output_tokens":832,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1431,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":832,"cache_read_input_tokens":939101,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1431},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLy6PCVLvcNTRhP8YrmW","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd544342-f422-4c3e-8816-8656a56f0596","timestamp":"2026-04-23T15:50:26.714Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
