{"parentUuid":"66f28269-abbd-47f4-af7c-3d055851635d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019KAWrYArgpom4r3mJi2wG5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the plan:\n\n---\n\n# Plan: pull attach-safety fixes out of `feat/entire-review` onto a branch from `main`\n\n## What to extract (standalone, not tied to reviews)\n\nAll four of these apply to **any** `entire attach` path — they currently work for plain attach on this branch because they're gated on `isExistingCheckpoint`, not on review mode. None of them require the `attachOptions` struct, the review-attach surfaces, or any review-specific machinery.\n\n### Fix 1 — Refresh `entire/checkpoints/v1` before attach (mirrors `entire resume`)\n\n**Problem**: `git pull` doesn't bring down the orphan `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch. If a colleague pushes a branch whose commits carry `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers and you attach to HEAD, the local metadata branch might not have the referenced checkpoint data.\n\n**Fix**: add `refreshForExistingCheckpoint(ctx, logCtx, repo, isExistingCheckpoint) *git.Repository` that, when HEAD has a trailer, calls `getMetadataTree(ctx)` from `resume.go`. This chains checkpoint-remote → treeless-fetch → local → full-fetch → remote-tracking ref, re-opening the repo between steps so go-git sees fresh packfiles. Non-fatal on fetch failure — logs a warn and returns the original repo.\n\n**Call site**: in `runAttach`, right after `resolveCheckpointID(headCommit)`, before `cpkg.NewGitStore(repo)`:\n\n```go\nrepo = refreshForExistingCheckpoint(ctx, logCtx, repo, isExistingCheckpoint)\nstore := cpkg.NewGitStore(repo)\n```\n\n**Reference commit on this branch**: `874f9a4ba` has the helper definition; the call site was already in place from earlier work.\n\n### Fix 2 — Refuse attach when checkpoint is still missing after refresh\n\n**Problem**: if the fetch chain doesn't bring the checkpoint in (colleague never pushed metadata, checkpoint_remote unreachable, branch came from someone else entirely), the attach would silently create a fresh checkpoint with the same ID as HEAD's trailer. On push, that clobbers the colleague's session data.\n\n**Fix**: add `verifyCheckpointLocallyAvailable(ctx, store, checkpointID, isExistingCheckpoint) error`. Calls `store.ReadCommitted(checkpointID)`:\n\n- `summary != nil` → checkpoint present, continue.\n- `summary == nil, err == nil` → refuse with a concrete error pointing at `git fetch origin entire/checkpoints/v1:entire/checkpoints/v1` and noting that the colleague may need to push metadata first.\n- `err != nil` → propagate wrapped.\n\nOnly runs when `isExistingCheckpoint == true`. Fresh checkpoints (no trailer) are still created freely.\n\n**Call site**: immediately after `store := cpkg.NewGitStore(repo)`:\n\n```go\nif err := verifyCheckpointLocallyAvailable(ctx, store, checkpointID, isExistingCheckpoint); err != nil {\n    return err\n}\n```\n\n**Reference commit**: `874f9a4ba`.\n\n### Fix 3 — Overwrite tripwire in `writeStandardCheckpointEntries`\n\n**Problem**: an unreproduced production report had session 0 silently replaced with a different sessionID's data. `findSessionIndex` returns 0 when `existingSummary` is nil, which is intended for fresh checkpoints but becomes dangerous if `entries` already has session-0 metadata for some other reason (stale tree read, race).\n\n**Fix**: at the end of `writeStandardCheckpointEntries`, if `sessionIndex == 0` and `entries` has a pre-existing session-0 metadata with a *different* sessionID, log a loud `WARN` with checkpoint ID, existing sessionID, writing sessionID, and whether `existingSummary` was nil. One map lookup + one blob read; no-op on all non-index-0 writes.\n\n**Location**: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go`, in `writeStandardCheckpointEntries`, right before `return s.writeCheckpointSummary(...)`.\n\n**Reference commit**: `40681ab7b`.\n\n### Fix 4 — `defer logging.Close()` in `runAttach`\n\n**Problem**: `runAttach` calls `logging.Init` but doesn't defer `logging.Close`, so the 8KB buffered writer never flushes on process exit. Any `Warn`/`Info` during attach gets silently dropped. Matters for Fix 3's tripwire — otherwise a warning fires but is invisible.\n\n**Fix**: add `defer logging.Close()` immediately after `logging.Init`. Matches the pattern in `resume`, `clean`, `reset`, `rewind`, `migrate`, `explain`.\n\n**Reference commit**: `40681ab7b`.\n\n## Tests to port\n\nPort these from this branch. The test *subject* is attach safety, not reviews — just drop the `Review: true` / skills arguments when porting:\n\n- **Missing-checkpoint refusal**: port `TestAttach_ReviewRefusesWhenCheckpointMissingFromLocalBranch` as `TestAttach_RefusesWhenCheckpointMissingFromLocalBranch`. Amend HEAD with a synthetic `Entire-Checkpoint: ffffffffeeee` trailer that points at nothing local. Call `runAttach` (plain, no review). Assert err fires with the \"missing from the local entire/checkpoints/v1 branch\" + fetch-command strings. Assert no fresh checkpoint was written for that ID. Also includes the `runGitInDir` helper using `exec.CommandContext`.\n\n- **Append-doesn't-overwrite**: port `TestAttach_ReviewAppendsAsAdditionalSessionWhenIDDiffers` as `TestAttach_AppendsAsAdditionalSessionWhenIDDiffers`. First attach creates checkpoint with session A; second attach with different session ID. Assert both sessions present on the summary. (Passes on this branch — pins the happy-path append path.)\n\n- **Tripwire**: new test in `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed_test.go` that constructs an `entries` map with session-0 metadata for `session-old`, calls `writeStandardCheckpointEntries` with `opts.SessionID = \"session-new\"` and no `existingSummary` in entries, then reads the captured log output and asserts the WARN fired. (There is no such test on this branch — would be a good add on the new branch.)\n\n- **Log-flush sanity**: optional. `entire attach` in a fresh repo, grep `.entire/logs/entire.log` for the `logging.Init` log line. Proves the writer actually flushed.\n\n## Execution\n\nFrom `main`:\n\n```bash\ngit switch main\ngit pull\ngit switch -c soph/attach-checkpoint-safety\n\n# Then either cherry-pick or hand-copy:\n# - 40681ab7b for the tripwire + defer logging.Close\n# - 874f9a4ba for the refresh + missing-checkpoint guard\ngit cherry-pick 40681ab7b 874f9a4ba\n```\n\nCherry-picks will likely have conflicts because the context around `runAttach` differs (your branch added `attachOptions` and the review-attach surfaces). Resolve by keeping only the shared pieces:\n\n- `attach.go`: keep `refreshForExistingCheckpoint`, `verifyCheckpointLocallyAvailable`, `defer logging.Close()`, and the two call sites. Skip `attachOptions`, `opts.Review` branches, `runAttachSurfaceReviewErrors`, `resolveReviewSkills`. `runAttach`'s signature stays as `(ctx, w, sessionID, agentName, force bool)` — the two helpers don't need opts at all.\n- `committed.go`: take the tripwire block as-is (it doesn't reference anything review-specific).\n- `attach_test.go`: take `runGitInDir` + the missing-checkpoint test, drop the `Review:`/`ReviewSkillsOverride:` fields from the `attachOptions{...}` literal — on main, use `runAttach(ctx, w, sessionID, agentName, true /* force */)`.\n\nAlternatively, skip cherry-pick entirely and just hand-write the six helpers + four call sites + tests against `main`'s current `runAttach` shape. The total surface is small enough (~120 lines of code + ~80 lines of test) that hand-writing avoids conflict mess.\n\n## What stays behind on `feat/entire-review`\n\nThe review-attach-specific additions stay with the review feature and land with it:\n\n- `attachOptions` struct\n- `resolveReviewSkills` helper\n- `runAttachSurfaceReviewErrors` wrapper\n- `opts.Review && isExistingCheckpoint` session-already-in-checkpoint guard\n- `entire review attach <id>` subcommand\n- `--review` and `--skills` flags on `entire attach`\n- All `TestAttach_Review*` tests\n\nNone of those depend on the safety fixes — the safety fixes sit *under* them. Once the safety PR lands on `main`, rebasing `feat/entire-review` onto the new `main` should be a clean rebase for attach.go (your review additions will just sit on top).\n\n## Risk check\n\n**The safety fixes apply to every attach, including ones that were working fine today.** Worth one round of manual testing on `main` before merging the new branch:\n\n1. Plain `entire attach <id>` in a repo with an up-to-date local checkpoints branch — should be unchanged.\n2. Plain `entire attach <id>` in a repo where HEAD has a trailer pointing at a checkpoint NOT in the local branch — should now print the \"missing from the local entire/checkpoints/v1 branch\" error and refuse. (This is a behavior change. Worth calling out in the PR description.)\n3. Plain `entire attach <id>` in a repo where the fetch can pull the missing checkpoint — should fetch, succeed.\n\nWant me to draft the commit messages / PR description for the new branch too, or just this plan?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1863,"cache_read_input_tokens":941405,"output_tokens":3488,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1863,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3488,"cache_read_input_tokens":941405,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1863},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaLytHzErykrjHn4VmjGL","type":"assistant","uuid":"33adb0bd-1208-46aa-aa4c-1a6e78f4d377","timestamp":"2026-04-23T16:01:17.230Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"9a29d9ba-5e22-4e92-a5d0-017356e28328","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"feat/entire-review"}
