{"parentUuid":"48b78ef0-f596-4bbc-b568-dcdf126cd7d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01T3KSRTsbhLUv3LBtWG7Fvg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green. Review of the extraction:\n\n## What landed on `soph/attach-checkpoint-safety`\n\nTwo commits cleanly isolated from any review-feature coupling:\n\n**`3e4757ffd` — guard attach checkpoints** (`attach.go` + `attach_test.go`, +167 lines)\n- `defer logging.Close()` in `runAttach`\n- `refreshForExistingCheckpoint` helper + call site (mirrors `entire resume`'s fetch chain via `getMetadataTree`)\n- `verifyCheckpointLocallyAvailable` helper + call site (refuses when checkpoint missing after refresh, with the \"run `git fetch origin entire/checkpoints/v1:entire/checkpoints/v1`\" error message)\n- `TestAttach_AppendsAsAdditionalSessionWhenIDDiffers` (happy path: two sessions land at index 0 and 1)\n- `TestAttach_RefusesWhenCheckpointMissingFromLocalBranch` (synthetic trailer → attach refuses, no checkpoint written)\n- `runGitInDir` helper using `exec.CommandContext`\n- No `attachOptions`, no review references — plain `runAttach(..., force bool)` signature preserved.\n\n**`5a875d588` — warn on checkpoint overwrite** (`committed.go` + new `committed_tripwire_test.go`, +114 lines)\n- Session-0 tripwire in `writeStandardCheckpointEntries` — logs WARN when writing replaces a different sessionID at index 0\n- New `TestWriteStandardCheckpointEntries_WarnsOnUnexpectedSessionZeroOverwrite` at the package level\n\n## One real improvement in the extraction\n\nThe tripwire now **captures the pre-existing session-0 metadata BEFORE `writeSessionToSubdirectory` clears the subtree**, instead of reading it after. This matters because `writeSessionToSubdirectory` does:\n\n```go\nfor key := range entries {\n    if strings.HasPrefix(key, sessionPath) {\n        delete(entries, key)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n— which wipes the old entries at the target path before writing new ones. My original version on `feat/entire-review` read `entries[basePath+\"0/metadata.json\"]` *after* the write, so it always saw the new sessionID and never fired. Yours saves the blob hash up front so the comparison actually works. Good catch. This is a functional bug fix I missed.\n\n## Test coverage sanity\n\n- `TestAttach_AppendsAsAdditionalSessionWhenIDDiffers` passes — the happy append path is pinned.\n- `TestAttach_RefusesWhenCheckpointMissingFromLocalBranch` passes — the missing-checkpoint guard is pinned.\n- `TestWriteStandardCheckpointEntries_WarnsOnUnexpectedSessionZeroOverwrite` passes — the tripwire actually fires (and with the bug in the original impl, it wouldn't have).\n- Full `mise run test:ci` green (52 canary + 4 external-agent + all unit/integration).\n- Lint clean.\n\n## What to check in the PR\n\nThe behavior change worth calling out explicitly: previously `entire attach` in a fresh-pulled branch would silently create a checkpoint if the trailer pointed at one that wasn't in local `entire/checkpoints/v1`. Now it refuses and tells the user to fetch. Anyone with a workflow relying on the old behavior (hard to imagine a correct one) will see this as a regression. The error message is self-explanatory, so it should be a net improvement.\n\nReady to push/PR from your side whenever."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":965645,"output_tokens":1229,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":226,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1229,"cache_read_input_tokens":965645,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":226},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaM1QpcvvCgU4AzEEFUnL","type":"assistant","uui